<Base title="About"><section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE PAGES</p><h1>Hello, I’m André<span class="rust">.</span></h1><p class="lede">This is a place to think out loud, follow a question,<br class="desktop-break"/> and leave a few notes for the next curious person.</p></section><div class="about-grid"><div class="prose"><h2>A little room for curiosity</h2><p>I’m interested in how we make sense of things: the models we build, the tools we use, and the stories we tell ourselves when the evidence is incomplete.</p><p>This notebook brings those interests together. Some ideas need an essay. Others only need a paragraph. And some are best explored in the margins of a good book.</p><blockquote>The aim is to understand a little more, and to be a little less certain.</blockquote><h2>What you’ll find here</h2><p><a href="/articles/">Articles</a> follow an idea in depth. <a href="/signals/">Signals</a> collect smaller observations. <a href="/books/">Books</a> hold reading notes and questions worth returning to.</p><h2>About this first edition</h2><p>This biography and every entry are sample content, ready to be replaced with your own words. The site is a local prototype, built with Astro and MDX.</p></div><aside class="margin-note"><span class="eyebrow">CURRENTLY THINKING ABOUT</span><ul><li>Probability as a way of seeing</li><li>Tools that make room for thought</li><li>The art of paying attention</li></ul><span class="handwritten">Stay curious. ↗</span></aside></div></Base>
